  "what_this_shows": "The routed netlist behaves identically to RTL with the extracted, corner-specific path delays applied and the tests' host timing (inputs change on the falling edge). Setup failures would appear as wrong captured data when a path exceeds the period; STA reports 57 ns of setup margin, consistent with no failures.",
  "limitations": [
    "Icarus Verilog ignores SDF timing checks, so setup/hold limits and notifier-driven X are not exercised; hold margins are covered only by STA (+0.113 ns worst at the fast corner).",
    "INTERCONNECT delays are annotated by Icarus only partially; STA remains the signoff for timing.",
    "Zero-delay UDP flip-flop models; no metastability or analog effects."
  ],
  "tools": {
    "iverilog": "12.0",
    "cocotb": "2.0.1",
    "python": "3.12"
  }
